From b8564c33caeaf0c2ac3fed29dcfff47c13e7512c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:51:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 101/142] OdfFile: do not read current_font_size.back() on an
 empty vector

Converting a docx that holds a form content control crashes the ODF
writer with SIGSEGV when no font size has been resolved yet.

DocxConverter::convert(OOX::Logic::CSdt*) reaches
calculate_font_metrix(L"Arial", current_font_size.back(), ...) inside the
"if (!width)" branch of the form path. current_font_size is empty until a
run or the document defaults push onto it, so on a docx whose styles
state no size the load addresses __end_ - 1 and the process dies. This is
the only unguarded read of that vector in the file: :728 and :3802 both
test empty() first, and MathConverter.cpp:170 and :264 already carry the
intended fallback.

The branch is reached by exactly the control types that do not set their
own width, so date, plain text, rich text and checkbox all crash while a
drop-down list and a combo box escape. It is not a hypothetical input:
converting a flat ODF document to OOXML produces a styles.xml with an
empty <w:docDefaults> and no <w:sz> anywhere, so x2t writes a file it
then cannot read back.

Reproduced on features.fodt and fields.fodt, which round-trip at exit 0
in their packaged .odt form and exit 139 in their flat form, the only
difference being whether the generated styles.xml carries a <w:sz>.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
index 76b188344f..2e5617979f 100644
--- a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
+++ b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
@@ -678,7 +678,11 @@ void DocxConverter::convert(OOX::Logic::CSdt *oox_sdt)
 
 		if (!width)
 		{
-			odf_context()->calculate_font_metrix(L"Arial", current_font_size.back(), false, false, true);
+			// current_font_size is empty until a run or the document defaults
+			// resolve one. A form control can be reached before that happens,
+			// for instance in a docx whose styles state no size at all.
+			double base_font_size = current_font_size.empty() ? 12. : current_font_size.back();
+			odf_context()->calculate_font_metrix(L"Arial", base_font_size, false, false, true);
 			std::pair<double, double> font_metrix = odf_context()->font_metrix();
 
 			width = font_metrix.first * value.length();
